{
  "dom_id": "step-q354520",
  "name": "Question 9",
  "problem": "An artist painted $60$ portraits last year. This year, her output is $400%$ greater than last year. How many portraits did the artist paint this year?\n\nThe artist painted\n{{field-1}}\nportraits this year.",
  "worked_solution": "To find this year's portrait output, we apply a $400%$ increase to last year's figure.\n\nIncreasing by $400%$ means that we must apply a new percentage of\n\n$$\n100%+400%=500%.\n$$\n\nWe begin by converting the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n500%=\\frac{500}{100}=5\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply the original amount by $5:$\n\n$$\n60\\times 5=300\n$$\n\nSo, the artist painted $300$ portraits this year.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
